      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really thoughtful advice, thanks. Changing topics\u2014could you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals? Nothing that\u2019ll stress my hand.",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some low-impact sports and activities you can consider while your finger heals:\n\n1. **Walking or Light Hiking**: Enjoy nature and get some exercise without stressing your hands.\n\n2. **Swimming**: This is a great full-body workout that minimizes strain on your hands. Just be cautious with strokes that require grip.\n\n3. **Cycling**: If you can manage the handlebars comfortably, cycling is a good option. You might want to consider padded gloves for added comfort.\n\n4. **Yoga or Tai Chi**: These practices can improve flexibility and strength without putting pressure on your fingers.\n\n5. **Pilates**: Focuses on core strength and stability, which can be done without using your hands extensively.\n\n6. **Gentle Stretching**: Incorporate stretches that don\u2019t involve your fingers to help maintain overall mobility.\n\nAlways listen to your body and consult with a healthcare professional if you're unsure about starting any new activity.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0028-27-00712:0": -0.6929513216018677
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
