            "I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years;",
            "Many years ago I had a bad fall while bouldering;"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Cold water can inhibit circulation and may not be ideal for recovery, especially if you're dealing with an injury like a finger injury. It can lead to reduced dexterity and increased discomfort, which might hinder your healing process. While swimming can be a low-impact exercise, it's important to consider how your finger feels in the water. If you experience any pain or discomfort while swimming in cold water, it would be best to avoid it until your finger heals. You might want to focus on warmer water activities or other low-impact exercises that don't strain your hand. Always consult with a healthcare professional if you're unsure about your recovery process.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0021-39-02570:0": -0.3390668034553528
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense. Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some great swimming spots near London where you can enjoy a swim while your finger heals:\n\n1. **London Aquatics Centre** - Located in Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park, this facility features a 50m pool and is great for all swimming levels.\n2. **Clapham Common Lido** - An outdoor swimming pool that offers a refreshing swimming experience in a scenic park setting.\n3. **Brockwell Lido** - A historic outdoor lido in Herne Hill, perfect for a relaxing swim during warmer weather.\n4. **Hampstead Heath Ponds** - These natural swimming ponds offer a unique outdoor swimming experience surrounded by nature.\n5. **Crystal Palace National Sports Centre** - Features a large swimming pool and various other sports facilities.\n\nMake sure to check the water temperature and conditions before heading out, especially given your finger injury. Enjoy your swim!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0000-36-01240:0": -1.2379016876220703
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in London, but my family is from Manchester"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Do you have advice on what budget I should consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For swimming in pools around London, you can expect to pay around \u00a35 to \u00a330 for a day pass, depending on the facility and its amenities. For example, places like the London Aquatics Centre typically charge around \u00a35.40 for a day pass, while more upscale gyms like Rena London St. Pauls may charge up to \u00a330. If you're considering a membership, prices can range from about \u00a335 to \u00a3100 per month, depending on the gym's location and facilities. It's a good idea to check for any corporate discounts or family packages, especially since you have children.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-74-01796:0": -0.9441850781440735
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks. What budget would you recommend if I try out yoga classes in London instead?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For yoga classes in London, you can expect to budget around \u00a310 to \u00a325 per class for drop-in sessions. If you prefer a membership, monthly fees typically range from \u00a340 to \u00a3100, depending on the studio and the number of classes included. Some studios also offer introductory deals for new students, which can be a great way to try out different classes at a lower cost.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0018-63-02654:2": 0.131382018327713,
            "clueweb22-en0024-37-13381:2": 0.1284482479095459,
            "clueweb22-en0001-43-13805:1": 0.09541112184524536
