      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, cheers. Actually, is it true that cold water isn\u2019t good for recovery? Should I avoid swimming while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "It's true that cold water may not be the best for recovery, especially after workouts. Some studies suggest that cold water immersion can delay muscle recovery and even increase soreness due to the release of catabolic hormones. If you're healing from an injury, like your finger, it's generally advisable to avoid swimming in cold water, as it might not support your recovery process. Instead, consider gentler activities that won't strain your finger, and if you want to swim, warm water might be a better option for your healing.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0044-53-03307:3": -2.3950846195220947
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
