      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense. Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are several great swimming spots near London where you can enjoy some time in the water. Here are a couple of options:\n\n1. **Frensham Great Pond, Farnham**: This family-friendly spot features a wide open lake with sandy bays, making it perfect for a day out. The calm waters are shallow for quite a distance, ideal for paddling, and there are facilities like a caf\u00e9 and changing rooms. It's about a 1.5-hour drive from London.\n\n2. **Ensfield Bridge, Tonbridge**: For a more natural swimming experience, you can swim in the River Medway near Ensfield Bridge. It's a peaceful spot with grassy banks to relax on after your swim. You can reach it in about 30 minutes by train from London Bridge.\n\nBoth locations offer a nice escape from the city, especially on warm days. Just make sure to check the conditions and ensure your finger is comfortable with swimming.",
