      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for asking, but I\u2019m good! I\u2019m more curious about new activities. Do you know anything that could lift someone\u2019s mood if they\u2019ve been feeling down?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some ways to help someone that is feeling blue for a while?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are several activities you can try to lift your mood if you're feeling down. Here are some suggestions:\n\n1. **Engage in Physical Activity**: Consider going for a walk, biking, or even trying yoga. Physical movement can help release endorphins and improve your mood.\n\n2. **Reconnect with Hobbies**: Dive back into activities you used to enjoy, such as visiting art museums or listening to jazz music. Engaging in things you love can bring joy and fulfillment.\n\n3. **Social Connections**: Spend time with friends or family, even if you don\u2019t feel like it initially. Social interactions can significantly boost your mood.\n\n4. **Try Something New**: Experiment with new activities, like taking a dance class or trying out a new recipe. This can help break the routine and introduce excitement.\n\n5. **Enjoy Music and Movies**: Put on your favorite tunes and dance around, or watch a lighthearted movie. These can be great ways to escape and uplift your spirits.\n\n6. **Volunteer**: Helping others through volunteer work can enhance your self-worth and connect you with your community.\n\n7. **Mindfulness and Meditation**",
