          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Cold water immersion, such as swimming, can have mixed effects on recovery. While cold water can reduce inflammation and pain temporarily, some studies suggest it might delay muscle recovery or interfere with beneficial adaptations from exercise. For your finger injury, swimming itself is unlikely to worsen recovery unless the water temperature is extremely cold, which could lead to stiffness or discomfort. If you enjoy swimming and the water is moderately cool, it might still be a good option for gentle exercise. However, if you\u2019re concerned, you could focus on other activities like cycling or yoga until your finger heals fully. Let me know if you\u2019d like more tailored advice!",
