          "user_utterance": "That sounds tempting. What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Swimming pool costs near London can vary depending on the facility and membership type. For example, London Fields Lido offers pay-and-play options starting at \u00a35.25 per adult per visit, with discounts for members and concessions. Monthly memberships are also available for regular swimmers. Alternatively, The Greenwich Centre provides flexible memberships, including swim-only options, with prices tailored to your needs. If you prefer occasional visits, pay-as-you-go rates are available at many pools, typically ranging from \u00a34 to \u00a36 per session. For more affordable options, some leisure centers offer free swimming for specific groups, such as Hackney residents under 18 or over 60. Exploring local council-run pools or checking platforms like Better can help you find the best fit for your budget and schedule.",
