            "I have two children."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you, that's really helpful. I\u2019ll keep that in mind. Switching topics a bit, could you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To stay active while your finger heals, it's best to avoid sports that could reinjure or stress your hand. Low-impact activities such as walking, cycling, and swimming are excellent options\u2014they provide cardiovascular benefits and are easy on the joints, with minimal involvement of the fingers [DOC-3]. You should take a break from activities that risk further injury, and only return to hand-intensive sports once your finger is fully recovered. If you do resume any activity that might involve your hand, consider using buddy taping for extra support until your finger is completely healed [DOC-4]. Are you interested in indoor or outdoor sports options?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-24-11847:0": 0.031024531024531024,
            "clueweb22-en0031-65-16720:2": 0.029850746268656716,
            "clueweb22-en0000-27-13761:0": 0.01639344262295082,
