      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sure, that would be useful. Also, do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For outdoor activities, protect your healing finger by using waterproof bandages or finger condoms, which help keep the wound dry and shielded from bacteria during activities like swimming or washing hands. Replace the bandage after each activity to maintain cleanliness and promote healing [clueweb22-en0012-66-16554]. In London, you have several excellent outdoor swimming options: Hampstead Heath Swimming Ponds offer a unique wild swimming experience, though the water can be chilly even in summer; Hampton Pool is a heated open-air pool, making it more comfortable for those who prefer warmer water; and West Reservoir in Hackney provides monitored open water swimming with facilities like hot showers and mandatory wetsuits for added protection [clueweb22-en0023-06-14225][clueweb22-en0017-19-07439][clueweb22-en0029-07-14670]. Always check the specific rules and book ahead, as many venues require reservations. Do you want information on swimming clubs or lessons in London?",
          "citations": {
