      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s really helpful. Before that\u2014what budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For most outdoor swimming pools and lidos in London, adult entry typically ranges from \u00a34 to \u00a310 per session. For example, Hampstead Heath Ponds charge \u00a34 for adults and \u00a32.40 for concessions, while West Reservoir in Hackney offers 50-minute open water sessions for \u00a310, bookable via the Better UK app. London Fields Lido and Britannia Leisure Centre both charge \u00a35.25 for non-member adults, with discounts for pay-and-play members (\u00a33.70) and further concessions (\u00a31.40). Some pools, especially in Hackney, offer free swimming for residents who are under 18, over 60, disabled, or carers, provided you register for a membership card. Heated pools like Hampton Pool may have slightly higher prices, but most public lidos and pools fall within this general range. Always check the venue's website for the latest prices and booking requirements before you go. Are you interested in monthly or annual membership options for regular swimming?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0012-66-17212:0": 0.031746031746031744,
            "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:1": 0.031544957774465976,
