        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019m thinking more about yoga now. What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For in-person or livestreamed yoga in London, drop-in classes usually cost between \u00a38 and \u00a315 per session, depending on the studio. For example, One Yoga London charges \u00a315 for a single class, while Psycle offers classes at \u00a312 each. If you plan to attend regularly, monthly memberships are a better value: East of Eden offers digital membership at \u00a324.99 per month, and Supply Yoga's monthly membership starts at \u00a335, often including unlimited access to classes. Online-only options can be even cheaper, with Frame offering on-demand classes from \u00a36 per month (with a yearly commitment) and live-streamed classes at \u00a37 each. Some studios, like Paper Dress Yoga, have live Zoom classes starting from just \u00a34. Outdoor yoga sessions, when available, are often priced similarly to drop-in studio classes. Always check for introductory offers or free trials, which many studios provide for new members [clueweb22-en0026-11-16076]. Are you interested in online yoga platforms for home practice?",
