    "topic": "3-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for asking! Actually, I\u2019m curious about ways people lift their mood if they\u2019ve been feeling blue for a while. Any suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some ways to help someone that is feeling blue for a while?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Evidence-based strategies for improving mood include starting and maintaining an exercise routine, as physical activity is closely linked to better mood and overall well-being. Even small actions, like taking the stairs or stretching during your desk job, can help [DOC-1][DOC-2]. Social connection is also important\u2014talking to trusted friends, family, or colleagues can provide support and perspective [DOC-2]. Music is another powerful tool; creating a playlist that gradually shifts from slower to more upbeat jazz or other favorite genres can help lift your spirits [DOC-2]. Structuring your day, getting better sleep, and accepting imperfections are additional tips recommended by mental health experts [DOC-3][DOC-4]. Are you interested in mindfulness or relaxation techniques for mood improvement?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0046-51-18606:2": 0.029273504273504274,
            "clueweb22-en0012-01-12975:4": 0.02750455373406193,
            "clueweb22-en0003-30-06140:0": 0.026151315789473682,
            "clueweb22-en0000-02-09450:0": 0.01639344262295082
