          "text": "For water-based rehab during finger recovery, focus on exercises that keep your hand relaxed and avoid gripping\u2014perfect for your climbing background and need for gentle, meaningful movement.\n\n**Top Water-Based Rehab Exercises (Finger-Friendly):**\n\n- **Gentle Water Walking/Jogging:** Move through chest-deep water, swinging arms gently with open hands. This boosts circulation and overall mobility without finger strain.\n- **Backstroke Swimming:** As discussed, this stroke keeps hands relaxed and avoids pressure on your fingers.\n- **Aquatic Resistance Band Work:** Use water-safe resistance bands with loops for hands/feet (see clueweb22-en0011-63-15243). You can anchor the band with your forearm or wrist, focusing on shoulder and arm movement while keeping fingers neutral.\n- **Hand Mobility in Water:** With your arm submerged, slowly open and close your hand, or gently spread and bring together your fingers. The water\u2019s resistance supports safe, low-impact movement (clueweb22-en0019-15-16622).\n- **Floating Arm Raises:** Hold a small float or noodle under",
