          "user_utterance": "These exercises sound helpful! Do you have advice on how to get started with these in the water? Any tips for a beginner?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To get started with water-based rehab as a beginner\u2014especially with your climbing background and focus on healing\u2014follow these steps for a safe, effective experience:\n\n**1. Choose the Right Pool**\n- Opt for a warm pool (ideally 92\u201395\u00b0F); warm water relaxes muscles and supports joint mobility, which is ideal for injury recovery (clueweb22-en0035-34-02011, clueweb22-en0023-82-13983).\n\n**2. Begin with a Gentle Warm-Up**\n- Start with slow water walking or gentle arm swings to acclimate your body and increase circulation (clueweb22-en0005-58-04448).\n\n**3. Focus on Form, Not Force**\n- Keep your hands relaxed and avoid gripping. For backstroke or water walking, let your fingers stay loose and open.\n- Use floatation devices (like a noodle or kickboard) if you need extra support\u2014just avoid squeezing them tightly (clueweb22-en0035-16-03774).\n\n**4. Progress Gradually**\n- Start with",
