          "user_utterance": "A sample weekly plan would be really helpful! What do you recommend?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Here\u2019s a sample weekly plan for water-based rehab that fits your climbing background, healing finger, and preference for restorative, meaningful activity:\n\n**Sample Weekly Water-Based Rehab Plan**\n\n**2\u20133 Sessions per Week (30\u201340 min each):**\n\n- **Warm-Up (5\u201310 min):**\n  - Gentle water walking or slow arm swings with relaxed hands (boosts circulation, preps joints).\n\n- **Main Set (20\u201325 min):**\n  - **Backstroke swimming:** 5\u201310 min, focus on relaxed, open hands.\n  - **Water walking/jogging:** 5\u201310 min, arms swinging gently, no gripping.\n  - **Hand mobility in water:** 5 min, slowly open/close fingers, spread/bring together\u2014water supports gentle movement.\n  - **Floating arm raises:** 5 min, use a noodle or float under forearms (not gripped), raise/lower arms for shoulder mobility.\n\n- **Cool-Down (5 min):**\n  - Gentle stretching in water, especially for shoulders and back.\n\n**Rest",
