      {
        "turn": 11,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "This plan looks perfect, thanks! Would you suggest any specific stretches for cooling down after my water sessions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For cooling down after your water-based rehab sessions\u2014especially with your climbing background and finger recovery\u2014prioritize stretches that restore mobility, promote blood flow, and gently target climbing-prone areas without stressing your healing finger.\n\n**Best Cool-Down Stretches for You:**\n\n- **Wrist and Finger Flexor Stretch:** Extend your arm, palm up; gently bend fingers down with your other hand until you feel a stretch (hold 20\u201330 sec). This maintains finger and forearm flexibility without strain (clueweb22-en0007-15-09796, clueweb22-en0031-34-05565).\n- **Prayer Stretch:** Palms together in front of chest, fingers up; slowly lower hands toward waist to stretch wrists and forearms (hold 20\u201330 sec).\n- **Chest Opener:** Interlace fingers behind your back, straighten arms, and gently lift to open chest and shoulders\u2014great for posture after swimming (clueweb22-en0025-10-08814, clueweb22-en0012-91-02347).\n-",
          "citations": {
