      {
        "turn": 12,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "These stretches sound excellent! Should I also consider any breathing exercises while stretching?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Absolutely\u2014combining stretching with mindful breathing is highly recommended, especially for climbers and anyone recovering from injury.\n\n**Why Add Breathing Exercises?**\n- Deep, controlled breathing during stretching increases oxygen flow, promotes relaxation, and helps release muscle tension (clueweb22-en0006-03-14924).\n- Techniques like diaphragmatic or \u201cbelly\u201d breathing support lung health and enhance the calming, restorative effects of your cool-down (clueweb22-en0005-59-05905, clueweb22-en0040-87-05736).\n\n**How to Integrate:**\n- As you hold each stretch, inhale slowly through your nose, expanding your belly and chest.\n- Exhale gently and fully, allowing your body to relax deeper into the stretch.\n- Try holding each breath for a few seconds before exhaling for added relaxation.\n\nThis approach aligns with your climbing background and preference for meaningful, restorative movement. Would you like a step-by-step guide for a specific breathing technique to pair with your stretches?",
          "citations": {
