      {
        "turn": 13,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "A step-by-step guide on a breathing technique would be great! What do you recommend?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For your cool-down stretches, pairing them with a focused breathing technique will maximize relaxation and recovery\u2014especially valuable for climbers and anyone healing from injury.\n\n**Recommended Technique: Alternate Nostril Breathing (Nadi Shodhana)**\n\n- **Why:** Proven to calm the nervous system, reduce stress, and deepen relaxation\u2014ideal after physical activity and during recovery (clueweb22-en0029-13-01454, clueweb22-en0031-84-00656, clueweb22-en0026-77-07413).\n- **How:**\n  1. Sit comfortably with a straight spine.\n  2. Place your left hand on your lap. With your right hand, use your thumb to gently close your right nostril.\n  3. Inhale slowly through your left nostril.\n  4. Close your left nostril with your ring finger, release your right nostril, and exhale through the right.\n  5. Inhale through the right nostril, close it, and exhale through the left.\n  6.",
