      {
        "turn": 14,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds calming! How many cycles of this breathing should I aim for while stretching?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For Nadi Shodhana (alternate nostril breathing), aim for 5\u201310 cycles during your cool-down stretches. This range is widely recommended for calming the mind, balancing the nervous system, and enhancing relaxation\u2014without feeling overwhelming for a beginner (clueweb22-en0006-22-17275, clueweb22-en0032-80-04109).\n\n- **How to pace:** Each cycle (inhale left, exhale right, inhale right, exhale left) should be slow and steady. Focus on quality, not speed.\n- **Why this fits you:** This duration is enough to promote recovery and mental clarity after your water-based rehab, aligning with your preference for meaningful, restorative routines.\n\nIf you find 5\u201310 cycles easy and calming, you can gradually increase to 24 cycles or up to 4 minutes as you get comfortable (clueweb22-en0032-80-04109).\n\nWould you like guidance on combining this with a short meditation or tips for tracking your progress?",
