  {
    "runtag": "orga-gpt41mini-bm25-minilm-llama70b-nopersonal",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "3-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for asking, but I'm actually looking for ideas for new activities. Got any suggestions that might cheer someone up if they're feeling a bit blue?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some ways to help someone that is feeling blue for a while?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "There are many ways to cheer someone up. You could start by asking them if they want help, and then simply be there for them. Sometimes, people just need someone to listen to them. You could also",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0035-65-11935:0": 2.3269050121307373,
            "clueweb22-en0023-36-13963:13": 0.8291285037994385,
            "clueweb22-en0023-36-13963:12": 0.8128662109375,
            "clueweb22-en0025-89-18025:1": 0.04856278374791145,
            "clueweb22-en0023-36-13963:1": -0.2571074366569519
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "The last answer wasn\u2019t so helpful. Can you be more specific? Maybe some concrete activities or ideas, especially for someone who\u2019s been down for a while?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some ways to help someone that is feeling blue for a while?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When someone's been down for a while, it's essential to offer specific help. You could try taking them for a walk in nature, watching a favorite movie together, or even just sitting with them in silence. Sometimes, small gestures like cooking a comforting meal or running errands for them can make a big difference. If you're looking for more ideas, you could try journaling, practicing yoga, or listening to uplifting music together. The key is to be present and show you care, rather than just offering vague support. What do you think might work best for the person you're trying to help?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0010-35-06057:4": 4.363584518432617,
            "clueweb22-en0003-90-09513:0": 3.9251720905303955,
            "clueweb22-en0046-27-16263:1": 3.5522241592407227,
            "clueweb22-en0010-70-02591:16": 3.3393654823303223,
            "clueweb22-en0018-28-06545:0": 3.3045668601989746
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019m looking for new things to do myself! I\u2019ve been climbing for a few years, but I\u2019ve hurt my finger recently so I need new options. Can you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you help me figure out some options for sports to start while my finger heals?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Considering your climbing background, you might enjoy activities that are low-impact on your joints and fingers. Swimming, cycling, or rowing could be great options. These sports can help you maintain your overall fitness while allowing your finger to heal. You could also try cross-country skiing, snowshoeing, or in-line skating for a fun and challenging workout. Additionally, martial arts like karate, tai chi, or soo bahk do might interest you, as they focus on technique and movement rather than high-impact stress on your fingers. What sounds appealing to you?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0031-88-16339:6": 2.200201988220215,
            "clueweb22-en0015-71-10781:13": 2.0292866230010986,
            "clueweb22-en0038-68-12824:4": 1.7398357391357422,
            "clueweb22-en0021-66-06454:13": 1.5864113569259644,
            "clueweb22-en0013-93-15759:17": 1.5723295211791992
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Swimming and cycling do sound promising. I\u2019m wondering though, is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Cold water can actually be beneficial for recovery, as it can help reduce inflammation and pain. However, it's essential to consider your overall health and any underlying medical conditions before engaging in cold water swimming. If you're recovering from a finger injury, it's crucial to avoid any activities that may exacerbate the injury or cause further strain. In your case, swimming in warm or temperate water might be a better option, allowing you to maintain your fitness while minimizing the risk of further injury to your finger. It's always a good idea to consult with a medical professional before starting any new exercise routine, especially when recovering from an injury.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0010-24-03939:4": 2.1589953899383545,
            "clueweb22-en0010-24-03939:3": 1.9034507274627686,
            "clueweb22-en0006-06-16791:3": 1.1778594255447388,
            "clueweb22-en0008-37-04307:0": 0.37274518609046936,
            "clueweb22-en0003-18-07281:7": 0.3570954501628876
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik": "Do you know of any water spot near London to do swimming?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there are several water spots near London where you can go swimming. One option is Hampstead Heath, which has three ponds open to wild swimming. Another option is Beckenham Place Park, which has a restored swimming lake. Additionally, you can also consider River Ouse in Buckinghamshire, which is not too far from London and offers a scenic spot for swimming. Just remember to check the safety and accessibility of the spot before you go.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-02-05902:7": 6.555595397949219,
            "clueweb22-en0035-14-10039:0": 6.36460018157959,
            "clueweb22-en0009-55-08812:0": 5.242965221405029,
            "clueweb22-en0025-02-05902:5": 5.163860321044922,
            "clueweb22-en0025-02-05902:6": 4.8809285163879395
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great, thanks. What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The budget for swimming in a pool near London can vary depending on the location and facilities. Some pools may offer day passes for around \u00a35-\u00a310, while others may require a membership or cost upwards of \u00a320-\u00a330 per visit. If you're looking for a more luxurious experience, some high-end gyms and spas may charge \u00a350-\u00a3100 or more per visit. It's best to research specific pools and their pricing to find one that fits your budget. Additionally, some gyms and fitness centers may offer discounts or promotions, so it's worth inquiring about those as well.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-14-10799:0": 2.9521713256835938,
            "clueweb22-en0009-77-12043:0": 1.0664067268371582,
            "clueweb22-en0041-93-14527:0": 0.9614362716674805,
            "clueweb22-en0001-76-14416:0": 0.1673588752746582,
            "clueweb22-en0009-55-08812:0": -0.049485236406326294
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s useful, thanks. What about yoga? What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for yoga?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For yoga, you can expect to pay around \u00a310-\u00a320 per class, depending on the studio and location. Some yoga studios in London offer introductory packages or discounts for new students, which can range from \u00a320-\u00a350 for a set number of classes. Monthly membership options are also available, which can cost anywhere from \u00a350-\u00a3150 per month, depending on the frequency of classes and amenities offered. Additionally, some gyms and fitness centers may include yoga classes as part of their membership packages. It's worth noting that some yoga studios also offer free or low-cost classes, especially for beginners or those with limited budgets.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0010-67-01298:0": 3.6078453063964844,
            "clueweb22-en0019-90-08199:10": 3.176893711090088,
            "clueweb22-en0026-11-16076:5": 2.361185312271118,
