      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great suggestions! What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Considering you're looking to swim in a pool near London, you might want to factor in the cost of pool membership or day passes. The cost can vary depending on the pool and its location, but on average, a swimming pool costs between $40,000 and $60,000 to install, with the structure costing around $112,500. However, if you're looking to swim at a public pool or a gym, the cost is likely to be much lower, ranging from $800 to $1,200 per year for pool maintenance and heating. As for the cost of swimming itself, the average in-ground swimming pool costs around $21,919, but you can also consider public pools or gyms that offer swimming facilities at a lower cost. You might also want to consider the cost of a pool enclosure, which can range from $6,333 to $19,666. I hope this helps you plan your swimming budget! Let me know if you have any other questions. Best",
          "citations": {
