      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That answer wasn\u2019t very helpful, unfortunately\u2014it\u2019s all about building a pool, not actually going for a swim! Can you give more accurate info about what a single swim or a monthly membership would cost at a London pool?",
          "user_rubrik": "What budget should I consider for swimming in a swimming pool near London?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Considering your finger injury, it's great that you're looking for a low-impact activity like swimming. There are several public pools in London that offer affordable swimming options. For example, the Oasis Sports Centre in the West End has a heated lido that's open year-round, and a single swim costs \u00a36.15. Alternatively, you could consider the Aquatics Centre in Stratford, which has a 50m pool and offers a monthly membership for \u00a335. This will give you access to over 20 pools across London, including London Fields Lido, a heated outdoor swimming pool in Hackney. You could also try the Balham Leisure Centre, which has a 25m pool and offers a monthly membership for \u00a332. I hope this helps you find a pool that fits your budget! Let me know if you have any other questions. Best, [Your Name] Source: [insert source]  I hope this helps!  Let me know if you have any other questions",
