          "text": "Considering your love for climbing and the outdoors, you could invite the person to join you for a gentle climb or a walk in a nearby park. Being in nature can be uplifting. Alternatively, you could suggest visiting an art museum, as you enjoy them, and spend the day exploring and discussing the exhibits together. Sometimes, engaging in a shared activity can help take their mind off their worries and provide a sense of connection. You could also put on some jazz music and have a relaxed conversation over a cup of coffee. These small gestures can go a long way in lifting someone's mood.  Additionally, you could also suggest listening to a podcast together, as you enjoy listening to them when alone at home.  This could be a great way to spend time together and take their mind off their worries.  You could also invite them to your new flat and show them your small garden, this could be a great way to spend time together outdoors.  You could also suggest going for a bike ride,",
