          "text": "Given your injury, it's essential to avoid activities that may exacerbate the condition. Considering your love for outdoor activities and warm weather, you might enjoy swimming or kayaking, which are low-impact sports that don't require intense finger usage. Alternatively, you could try cycling, as you mentioned you used to bike a lot when you were younger. These activities can help you stay active while allowing your finger to heal. Just be sure to consult with a medical professional before starting any new exercise routine.   (",
