          "text": "You could consider sports that don't require a lot of grip strength or finger dexterity, such as swimming, cycling, or yoga. These activities can help you stay active while allowing your finger to heal. You could also try low-impact sports like walking or hiking, which are easy on the joints and don't require a lot of hand use. Additionally, you could try sports that involve your upper body, such as rowing or kayaking, which can be modified to accommodate a finger injury. What do you think?  (",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting\u2014about swimming, I heard cold water might not be good for recovery, especially for injuries like mine. Is it true I should avoid swimming while my finger is recovering?",
