          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "While some sources suggest cold water can reduce short-term pain and inflammation, others indicate it may delay muscle recovery, especially for chronic injuries, by inhibiting circulation and making muscles and tendons stiff. Cold water can also cause \"dead fingers\" or reduce dexterity. It might be beneficial to swim in warmer water or use warm water to loosen your fingers. Always consult your doctor or physical therapist for personalized advice on your specific injury.",
