      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sure! I usually enjoy climbing outdoors, but with my finger injury, I definitely need something with less strain on the hands. I used to bike a lot when I was younger. Walking or activities that aren\u2019t rough on the fingers could work. Anything come to mind?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is it true that cold water is not good for recovery, and I thus should not do swimming while recovering from my finger injury?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your finger injury, cycling is an excellent option, especially since you used to enjoy biking, as it primarily uses your legs. Walking and hiking are also great low-impact choices that are gentle on your fingers. For activities with no hand strain, consider swimming or other water sports like water aerobics.",
