          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Based on the provided information, there is no direct evidence suggesting that regular swimming in a typical leisure centre pool slows down the healing of finger pulley injuries. In fact, swimming is often considered an ideal rehabilitation tool for athletes recovering from injuries due to its low-impact nature, minimal strain on joints and muscles, and ability to promote nerve regeneration.",
