          "text": "Typical London yoga costs (rough guide):  - Drop-in classes: \u00a36\u2013\u00a318 (community/council classes \u00a36\u201310; private/boutique studios \u00a312\u201318).   - Multi-class blocks/passes: 5\u201310 classes \u00a330\u201390 (saves money vs drop-in).   - Monthly memberships/unlimited: \u00a330\u2013120/month (chains and community studios at lower end; boutique studios higher).   - Private 1:1 sessions: \u00a340\u2013100+ per hour (senior teachers at top end).   - Online subscriptions: \u00a35\u201320/month (good low-cost option, many offer trials).   - Equipment: mat \u00a315\u201360, blocks/strap \u00a310\u201330, comfy clothes \u00a320+.    If you plan 2\u20133 classes/week, a monthly pass often works out best; occasional swimmers benefit from pay-as-you-go or small blocks. Look for concessions, community classes, or first-class deals to try styles (restorative, chair, gentle Hatha) that avoid heavy hand loading while your finger heals.",
