          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019m curious about supporting someone feeling blue. Any simple ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some ways to help someone that is feeling blue for a while?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "That\u2019s thoughtful of you. Simple, effective ways to support someone feeling blue:  - Be present and listen: ask open questions (\u201cHow are you feeling?\u201d), reflect back, and resist fixing or minimizing (\u201cThat sounds really hard\u201d). - Offer small, practical help: bring a meal, do a chore, look after kids briefly, or help arrange an appointment. - Suggest gentle activities together: a short walk in the garden, a relaxed museum visit, or listening to soothing music or a favourite podcast\u2014nothing demanding. - Encourage routine: sleep, regular meals, light exercise, and small achievable goals. - Share resources: offer to help find a GP, therapist, or helpline; suggest crisis help immediately if they mention self-harm or suicidal thoughts. - Check in regularly and set boundaries: be consistent but also protect your own energy.  If you want, tell me a bit about the person and I can suggest a few personalised ways to help.",
