          "text": "Good idea to protect the finger \u2014 here are sport and exercise options that minimise hand/finger use, plus brief tips:  - Walking/hiking: outdoors in warm weather or around your garden; add gentle hill intervals. - Running or brisk walking: no hands needed; use good shoes. - Cycling: recumbent or stationary bike reduces handlebar load; avoid long road rides until healed. - Elliptical or stair-climber: low impact, minimal grip required. - Swimming/aqua exercises: aqua jogging or water aerobics are excellent; use a pull-buoy or focus on leg-only sets if needed. - Lower-body strength training: squats, lunges, leg press, calf raises \u2014 use machines that don\u2019t require gripping. - Tai chi or gentle balance work: low impact and hand-light. - Dance/cardio classes that don\u2019t require partner holds.  Practical tips: avoid exercises that cause pain or forceful gripping, consider a protective splint, and check with your GP/physio for any sport-specific restrictions.",
